('alict_00536', 11, 'ICT & Society, Security, E-commerce', 'Which of the following best describes phishing?', '["Gaining unauthorized access to a system by exploiting security weaknesses", "Repeatedly sending offensive messages to harass someone online", "Tricking users into giving personal info using fake emails or sites. jHdc ,nd", "Spreading false or harmful information to damage someone''s reputation", "Physically stealing computer hardware or storage devices"]'::jsonb, 3, '• Option 1: This option is incorrect. This describes which involves breaking into computer systems or networks without permission. Hackers often use software tools or exploit security flaws to gain access to sensitive control or cause disruptions', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'ICT & Society, Security, E-commerce', 2027, 536, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00537', 11, 'ICT & Society, Security, E-commerce', 'Which of the following advancements is most likely to define sixth-generation computers?', '["Full integration of quantum computing and artificial intelligence quantum", "Use of nanotechnology for ultra-fast processing", "Development of bio-computing and DNA-based storage DNA mdol", "Enhanced neural networks mimicking human brain functionality", "Complete elimination of cloud computing in favor of local processing"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Option 1: This is correct. The sixth generation is expected to be dominated by quantum computing and AI advancements. Current trends indicate that this combination is the most probable direction for the next generation of computers', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'ICT & Society, Security, E-commerce', 2027, 537, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00538', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'Which of the following best describes the role of an Information System (IS) in an organization?', '["It only stores raw data without processing it", "It helps in the and communication of information to support decision-making", "It functions the same as the internet by providing websites and search engines. th", "It is used only by IT departments and not accessible by other departments. th IT", "It is primarily used for artistic design and media production only. th m%Odk"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Option 1: Incorrect. While data storage is a part of an information it also includes and communication. Simply storing raw data without turning it into useful information is not enough for decision-making or organizational needs. This answer limits the true scope of IS', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 2027, 538, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00539', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'Which of the following is NOT a characteristic of information?', '["Accuracy", "Relevance", "Timeliness", "Completeness", "Complexity"]'::jsonb, 5, 'Complexity is not considered as a characteristic of information. • Accuracy ensures that information is correct and it has no mistakes. It affects the quality of information. • Relevance Data has to be relevant to the user and the purpose it serves', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 2027, 539, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00540', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'Which of the following scenarios demonstrates the "Golden Rule of Information" in action?', '["A company uses 10-year-old customer feedback to launch a new product. iud.ula kj ksIamdokhla", "A student relies on outdated textbooks to prepare for a technology exam", "A weather station publishes a weekly weather report instead of daily updates", "A hospital delays updating patient records until the end of the month. udih wjidkh olajd", "A stock trader makes decisions based on real-time market trends. fldgia"]'::jsonb, 5, 'Option 1: This violates the Golden Rule of Information because customer preferences change over time. Using outdated feedback may result in an unsuccessful product launch. ukdmhka Option 2: This also violates the rule because technology evolves rapidly', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 2027, 540, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00541', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'Choose the best answer that can be used to describe the functionality of analog computers', '["It is operated by a set of discrete values", "Operated by a set of frequently varying values over a certain range", "Operated by a set of discrete values and a set of frequently varying values", "They always show a minimal loss of electrical energy", "Data is stored as 0''s and 1''s"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Option 1: This is incorrect. Discrete values are characteristic of digital not analog ones. Analog computers deal with continuous data rather than discrete steps. Option 2: This is correct', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 2027, 541, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00542', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'What is the purpose of data validation in the data processing lifecycle?', '["To collect raw data from various sources", "To ensure data and reliability", "To present information in a usable format", "To retain data for future use", "To analyze and transform data into insights"]'::jsonb, 2, 'The correct answer is 2) To ensure data and reliability. Data validation is a critical step in the data processing lifecycle that involves verifying and checking the data to ensure it meets predefined quality criteria', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 2027, 542, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00543', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'Which of the following consist of correct sequence of Data Processing Life Cycle?', '["Data Input , Data Collecting , Data Processing , Data Storing , Data Output", "Data Collecting , Data Processing , Data Output", "Data Collecting , Data Input , Data Processing , Data Storing , Data Output", "Data Input , Data Collecting , Data Storing , Data Processing , Data Output", "Data Output"]'::jsonb, 3, 'The Data Processing Life Cycle is a systematic approach to transform raw data into meaningful and useful information. l%udkql+, Below are the stages involved 1. Data Collecting The first step is to gather raw data from various sources such as or logs', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 2027, 543, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00544', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'When is timely information is most crucial ?', '["Preparing a historical analysis report", "Creating predictions for future stock trends", "Calculating annual sales revenue months after year-end. jir wjidkfha udi miq", "Generating archival records for reference", "Storing data that is rarely accessed"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Option 1: This involves analyzing past so it does not require current or real -time information. The timeliness of data isn''t critical for this task. fuhg Option 2: This requires the latest information because stock trends change quickly', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 2027, 544, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00545', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'In the context of data what is the mode that involves immediate processing?', '["Offline Processing", "Real-time Processing", "Batch Processing", "Direct Processing", "Indirect Processing"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Offline In this data is processed at a later not immediately. 3) Batch Data is collected and processed in large batches at scheduled not in real-time', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 2027, 545, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00546', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'What is the primary purpose of consistency checks in data validation?', '["Ensure data falls within a specified range", "Verify that data is correctly formatted", "Maintain data integrity and coherence", "Encrypt sensitive data", "Detect data redundancy"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Correct answer: "Maintain data integrity and coherence". This follows from the standard definitions of data, information, and ICT processing concepts.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 2027, 546, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00547', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'What is the primary difference between volatile and non-volatile memory?', '["Volatile memory is larger in capacity", "Volatile memory retains data without power", "Non-volatile memory requires constant power", "Non-volatile memory retains data without power", "Volatile memory operates slower than non-volatile memory"]'::jsonb, 4, 'The primary difference between volatile and non-volatile memory lies in data • Volatile memory Requires constant power to retain data. Once the power is the data is erased. • Non-volatile memory Retains data even when power is turned making it ideal for long-term storage', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 2027, 547, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00548', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'Which of the following is true about structured and unstructured data?', '["Structured data refers only to numerical while unstructured data includes text and images", "Unstructured data can be easily stored in relational unlike structured data", "Structured data is highly organized and easily while unstructured data lacks predefined organization", "Both structured and unstructured data must be stored in the same format for analysis", "Structured data contains no unlike unstructured data"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Option 1: Incorrect. Structured data is not limited to numerical it can include text as long as it fits into a predefined schema. Unstructured often includes text and multimedia formats. l%uhlg Option 2: Incorrect', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 2027, 548, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00549', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'Which of the following accurately statement reflects a key difference between Big Data and traditional data in terms of data processing and analysis?', '["Big Data typically uses batch processing while traditional data is processed using real-time processing techniques. uyd", "Big Data requires high-speed data transfer and advanced analytical whereas traditional data can be processed with basic software and slower data transfer methods. uyd", "Big Data is always while traditional data is always structured and fits into relational databases. uyd", "Big Data analysis usually focuses on historical while traditional data analysis is more concerned with real-time data. uyd", "Big Data is exclusively used in academic while traditional data is used for business applications. uyd"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Correct answer: "Big Data requires high-speed data transfer and advanced analytical whereas traditional data can be processed with basic software and slower data transfer methods. uyd". This follows from the standard definitions of data, information, and ICT processing concepts.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 2027, 549, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00550', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'What is the correct order of validation methods used?', '["Presence check \u2192 Range check \u2192 Data type check", "Data type check \u2192 Range check \u2192 Presence check", "Data type check \u2192 Presence check \u2192 Range check", "Presence check \u2192 Data type check \u2192 Range check", "Range check \u2192 Presence check \u2192 Data type check mrdih \u2192"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Data Type Check Ensures that the input is of the correct type numbers instead of letters). Connection The first thief tried entering letters instead of but the vault rejected it immediately. Presence Check Ensures that the input is not left empty', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 2027, 550, '2027 Quiz Series')
