('alict_00551', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'Which of the following best defines the difference between data and information in the context of ICT?', '["Data is a collection of random while information is data organized meaningfully", "Data always has a clear while information does not", "Data is and information is unprocessed facts", "Data represents while information represents facts", "Data is derived from while information is used to make decisions"]'::jsonb, 1, '• Option 1: This definition accurately reflects the fundamental distinction between the two concepts', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 2027, 551, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00552', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'What type of data access method is used by magnetic tapes?', '["Random access", "Sequential access", "Direct access", "Index access", "Parallel access"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Magnetic tapes use sequential access as their primary data access method. This means that data is read or written in a linear one piece at a starting from the beginning of the tape and moving forward until the required data is found', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 2027, 552, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00553', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'Which of the following is NOT a valid reason for using different number systems in computing?', '["Efficient data representation", "Simplification of arithmetic operations", "Better visual representation of data", "Optimization of storage", "Direct interaction with humans"]'::jsonb, 5, 'Efficient data representation Number systems such as binary (base-2) and hexadecimal (base-16) allow data to be efficiently represented and processed by computers. For binary aligns naturally with the on of transistors in hardware', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 2027, 553, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00554', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'Why is DRAM considered dynamic?', '["It uses a dynamic programming architecture", "It requires periodic refreshing to maintain data", "Its capacity varies dynamically with system requirements. tys", "It supports dynamic reallocation of storage resources. th", "It operates dynamically across different voltage levels. th"]'::jsonb, 2, 'DRAM (Dynamic Random-Access Memory) is considered dynamic because it stores data in tiny which gradually lose their charge over time. To preserve the capacitors need to be periodically refreshed. DRAM ksid This periodic refreshing is what makes DRAM "dynamic', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 2027, 554, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00555', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'A government uses information and communication technology to communicate with their and other governments. rchla fhdod ;u mqrjeishka" iu. of the following is NOT a part of the relationship between government and business (G2B)?', '["Payment Services", "Bank Details", "Business Registration", "Election Result", "Business and Investments"]'::jsonb, 4, 'The E - government is divided into 4 parts. b - fldgia 4lg fnod 1. Services provided by a government to citizens rchlska mqrjeishkag imhk fiajd • Government institution catalog • Bill payment services • Renewal of Vehicle Licenses • Government Information Centre • Election Result 2', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 2027, 555, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00556', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'Which of the following is a major use of big data in predictive analytics?', '["Archiving historical data for future generations", "Developing mathematical formulas for basic calculations", "Forecasting consumer behavior patterns using machine learning", "Reducing data variety to improve consistency", "Organizing data into smaller subsets for manual analysis"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Option 1: While archiving is it doesn''t directly contribute to predictive analytics. Predictive analytics focuses on forecasting future not just storing data for future use', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 2027, 556, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00557', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'What does the term "offline input" refer to?', '["Data is entered continuously", "Data is processed in real-time", "Data is input after a specific time period", "Data is input with direct user interaction", "Data is automatically generated"]'::jsonb, 3, 'entry or typically after a certain period of rather than being processed immediately', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 2027, 557, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00558', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'Which of the following is a characteristic of special purpose computers?', '["The most powerful type of computer", "A large amount of data can be handled simultaneously", "10-15 terminals can be served simultaneously", "Cannot be reprogrammed", "It can perform any task that a computer can perform"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Special-purpose computers are designed to perform a specific task or set of tasks. Unlike general-purpose they are optimized for a single function and often cannot perform unrelated tasks. Explanation of each option 1: This is not correct for special -purpose computers', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 2027, 558, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00559', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'Which of the following is LEAST affected by using manual methods for data analysis?', '["Processing speed", "Data accuracy", "Data security", "Scalability for large datasets", "Data automation capability"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Option 1: Incorrect. Manual data analysis is significantly slower than automated methods since humans take more time to process and interpret data compared to computers. Option 2: Incorrect', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 2027, 559, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00560', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'Which of the following is NOT an example of the application of information in daily life?', '["Tracking fitness goals using wearable devices", "Searching for the nearest gas station on a smartphone. cx.u", "Managing finances using budget-tracking apps. whjeh", "Monitoring satellite orbits for interplanetary missions", "Reading weather forecasts to plan outdoor activities"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Option 1: This is a common daily where devices collect and display information like heart and calories burned. ffoksl l%shdldrluls" jeks Option 2: A routine use of GPS-based information systems for convenience in daily travel. ffoksl', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 2027, 560, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00561', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'Which of the following is the most critical challenge associated with managing big data?', '["Creating duplicate datasets for security", "Ensuring a constant influx of data at high speed", "Handling large volumes of diverse data formats", "Storing big data only in relational uyd", "Avoiding the use of distributed computing fnod ,o"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Option 1: False. While data backup and redundancy are important for security and duplication alone is not a major challenge in managing big data. managing redundant data efficiently without excessive storage costs is a concern. Option 2: False', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 2027, 561, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00562', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'Which of the following statements best describes the role of ICT in modern information systems?', '["ICT is limited to hardware and without influencing data processing and communication. ICT", "ICT enables the integration of and networks to enhance information processing and decision-making", "ICT only refers to the internet and digital excluding traditional computing devices", "ICT is primarily concerned with storing data and has no impact on communication technologies. ICT m%Odk", "ICT is only used in business environments and has no significant role in education or healthcare. ICT"]'::jsonb, 2, 'ICT plays a crucial role in modern information systems by combining and networks to facilitate data and decision -making. It is not limited to just hardware and nor is it solely about storage or internet-based communication', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 2027, 562, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00563', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'Which is not a disadvantage of using ICT in manufacturing industry?', '["Complexity", "Less accuracy", "Data Loss and Failures", "Initial and Ongoing Maintenance costs", "Environmental Impact"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Correct answer: "Less accuracy". This follows from the standard definitions of data, information, and ICT processing concepts.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 2027, 563, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00564', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'Which answer portrays the feature of data?', '["Meaningful", "Helps to make decisions", "Meaningless or less meaningful", "Can predict the future", "Conforms or renews previous knowledge"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Meaningful This describes not data. Data is the unprocessed facts. Meaning is derived from data after it''s organized and analyzed. lr 2) Helps to make decisions This is also a characteristic of information', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 2027, 564, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00565', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'Which of the following is an example of how big data benefits businesses?', '["Reducing the need for digital marketing strategies", "Helping companies predict market trends and consumer preferences", "Replacing structured databases with unstructured data", "Avoiding the use of cloud storage solutions", "Eliminating the role of data visualization tools"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Option 1: Incorrect. Big data does not reduce the need for digital by providing insights into customer and trends. Businesses use big data analytics to refine their digital marketing efforts and make them more effective. uyd ukdm Tjqkaf.a Option 2: Correct', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 2027, 565, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00566', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'What is the main distinction between data and information in a processing system?', '["Data is always and information is textual", "Data represents valuable while information is raw and unprocessed", "Data is only relevant for big data while information is for decision-making", "Data and information are synonymous in any system", "Data is the and information is the output"]'::jsonb, 5, 'the other is derived from processing and organizing data to provide context and meaning. For stating that "the average temperature over three days is 27°C" is information because it adds value and insight to the data', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 2027, 566, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00567', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'A teacher creates a program to calculate the total marks of a student. If a student enters "ten" instead of 10, an error is shown by the .Kkh jevigykla "oyh" jevigyk fmkajhs'' Which type of data validation would detect this error?', '["Range check", "Presence check", "Uniqueness check", "Length check", "Type check"]'::jsonb, 5, 'Option 1: Incorrect. This validation ensures that the input is within a specified range and verifies that the entered value falls within those bounds. Option 2: Incorrect. This validation checks if the input field has been filled and ensures no field is left blank', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 2027, 567, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00568', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'Choose the statement that is not true about qualitative information', '["Quality information helps in knowledge development", "Creating quality information costs more", "In zero the value of quality information is very high", "Uses accurate data to create quality information", "Quality information can be used for decision making"]'::jsonb, 3, 'The correct answer is 3) Uses accurate data to create quality information. This statement is incorrect because qualitative information focuses on non-numerical which includes and observations', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 2027, 568, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00569', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'Which of the following isn''t a feature of DRAM (Dynamic Random Access Memory)?', '["Ability to store large number of bits in a physically small area", "Loses data when power is turned off", "Requires periodic refreshing to maintain data", "Faster access speed compared to SRAM (Static Random Access Memory) SDAM", "Used to create the main memory. m%Odk"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Option 1: DRAM stores data using capacitors and allowing it to store more data per unit area compared to SRAM. option 1) is a feature of DRAM. DRAM Option 2: DRAM is a volatile meaning it requires power to retain data. When power is all stored data is erased', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 2027, 569, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00570', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'In computers assist in verifying medication information like drug labels and expiry dates. Which system is responsible for this?', '["Diagnostic System", "Patient Monitoring System", "Lab-Diagnostic System", "Pharmacy Information System", "Surgical Support System"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Diagnostic System This system assists in diagnosing medical conditions through data such as lab and patient history. It does not typically handle medication verification. u', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 2027, 570, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00571', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'Which of the following statements about data and information is incorrect?', '["Data is always meaningful and directly just like information", "Data consists of raw or whereas information is meaningful and organized data", "Data must be processed through or computation to become useful information", "The accuracy and reliability of information depend on the quality of the data used to generate it", "Information helps in whereas raw data alone may not be directly useful"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Option 1: Incorrect. Data is raw and meaning it may not always be meaningful or directly useful. It becomes useful only after processing. Option 2: Correct. Data is while information is processed and meaningful. Option 3: Correct', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 2027, 571, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00572', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'Which of the following is an advanced application of ICT (Information and Communication Technology) in agriculture that optimizes resource allocation?', '["Manually controlling irrigation times based on personal judgment", "Using simple soil testing kits for nutrient analysis", "Implementing machine learning models for predicting crop diseases fnda. frda", "Relying on historical yield data without real-time analysis", "Maintaining traditional farm equipment without sensors"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Machine learning (ML) is an advanced application of ICT in agriculture that significantly enhances decision-making by leveraging data-driven insights', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 2027, 572, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00573', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'Which of the following is a key characteristic of Big Data?', '["It only deals with structured data. th", "Traditional databases are sufficient for handling it", "It requires advanced tools for storage and analysis", "It does not need high-speed processing. thg", "Small-scale storage methods can handle Big Data efficiently. l%u uyd"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Option 1: This is incorrect. Big Data deals with all types of data semi and unstructured). It can include data from social sensor and much not just structured data. fndfyda foa Option 2: This is incorrect', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 2027, 573, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00574', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'What is a key benefit of ICT in education?', '["Increased physical activity", "Quick access to information", "Limited communication options", "Decreased use of technology", "Higher cost of learning"]'::jsonb, 2, 'ICT provides students and educators with fast and convenient access to vast such as research online and educational videos. ICT u', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 2027, 574, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00575', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'A retail company uses big data analytics to predict customer purchasing patterns. Which of the following is an example of how big data could help the company?', '["Offering the same discounts to all customers. tlu", "Predicting which a customer might buy next", "Storing customer data in a local spreadsheet", "Sending random promotional emails to customers", "Limiting stock to avoid overproduction entirely"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Option 1: This does not utilize big data analytics as it treats all customers equally without personalizing offers based on purchasing behavior', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 2027, 575, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00576', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'Which of the following is a limitation of the V on Neumann architecture?', '["It supports multi-threading for parallel task execution. th", "It requires separate memory for instructions and data. Wmfoia", "The V on Neumann bottleneck can lead to performance issues. V on Neumann bottleneck", "It uses a non-linear memory access pattern. th", "It has limited support for complex mathematical operations"]'::jsonb, 3, 'The V on Neumann architecture is a computer design model that uses a single memory for both instructions and data. While it is widely it has a key limitation known as the V on Neumann which can slow down performance due to limited data transfer between the CPU and memory', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 2027, 576, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00577', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'One of the fundamental principles of the V on Neumann architecture fjdka kshquka', '["Utilizing multiple processing units for parallel execution", "Storing both instructions and data in separate memory locations. Wmfoia", "Fetching and executing instructions sequentially from memory", "Employing a complex control unit for pipelined instruction processing", "Implementing a non-uniform memory access scheme"]'::jsonb, 3, 'The Von Neumann architecture is characterized by the use of a single address space for both instructions and data. This means that the CPU fetches instructions and data from the same memory unit', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 2027, 577, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00578', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'What is the purpose of a "file backup" in file management?', '["To create a duplicate of a file", "To restore lost files", "To protect against data loss", "All of the above", "None of the above"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Let''s consider each option one by one. Option 1: This is correct because a backup involves making a copy of the original file to ensure that data is available even if the original file is lost or corrupted', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 2027, 578, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00579', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'What is the name given to data consisting of descriptive characteristics that cannot be measured separately?', '["Quantitative data", "Qualitative data", "Discrete data", "Spatial data", "Structured data"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Quantitative Data This type of data is numerical and can be measured and counted. It includes data such as and which can be represented using numbers and often subjected to statistical analysis', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 2027, 579, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00580', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'Which of the following is an example of real-time processing?', '["Payroll calculation", "Billing system", "Automatic production line", "Data backup", "Batch data entry"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Option 1: This process typically happens such as weekly or and does not require immediate results after each data entry. it is not an example of real-time processing', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 2027, 580, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00581', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'Which of the following statements is false regarding QR codes?', '["QR code stands for Quick Recognition code. QR", "Some QR codes can track scanning information such as number of location etc. iuyr QR", "A type of two-dimensional matrix code", "Stores data both horizontally and vertically", "Has 3 squares allowing the scanning device to determine the orientation"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Option 1: This statement is false. The acronym "QR" in QR code stands for "Quick Response" not "Quick Recognition" code. Recognition" Option 2: It is true that certain QR codes can be encoded to track various types of scanning information', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 2027, 581, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00582', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'The age limit is represented from 19 to 22 when students are registered for university entrance via the website. Which of the following data validation method is most appropriate for this situation?', '["Type check", "Range check", "Numeric check", "Format check", "Presence check"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Option 1: The type check ensures that the data entered is of the correct data type. For it verifies that the input is numeric rather than text. While it confirms that the data is of a certain type (like numbers), it does not validate whether the numeric value falls within a specified range', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 2027, 582, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00583', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'Which of the following is a disadvantage of disk defragmentation?', '["Increased disk speed after defragmentation", "Requires a lot of system resources while running", "Improves file organization on the disk", "Can recover lost data", "Helps prevent disk wear and tear"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Disk defragmentation consumes a large amount of system resources such as CPU disk and memory while it is running. Because of the system can become and unresponsive during the especially on low-end computers', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 2027, 583, '2027 Quiz Series'),
