('alict_00737', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'If the ASCII value of is 66, How can we represent the word ''DEOGEN''?', '["01000100 01001111 01000111 01000101 01001110", "01000100 01000101 01001111 01000111 01000101 01001110", "01000100 01000101 01001100 01000111 01000101 01001110", "01000100 01000000 01001111 01000100 01000101 01001110", "01000111 01000101 01001111 01000100 01000101 01001111"]'::jsonb, 2, 'We need to find the binary ASCII representation of the word ''DEOGEN''. Let''s break it "DEOGEN" hk jpkfha D → ASCII value is (ASCII w.h) 68 → Binary E → ASCII value is (ASCII w.h) 69 → Binary O → ASCII value is (ASCII w.h) 79 → Binary G → ASCII value is (ASCII w', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 2027, 737, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00738', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', '8 bit 2''s complement of a decimal number called X is 110100012. What is the value of that X?', '["46", "-46", "47", "-47", "208"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Given the 2''s complement of a one bit must be subtracted from the second complement to find its first complement. fojk wvq 1 0 1 0 12 - 12 1 0 1 0 02 When finding the negative number corresponding to the first those bits must be inversed', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 2027, 738, '2027 Quiz Series'),
