('alict_00740', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'What is the binary equivalent to 0.62510 in decimal notation?', '["0.1112", "0.1012", "1.0102", "0.1002", "0.0012"]'::jsonb, 2, '0.625 × 2 = 1.250 ------- 1 0.250 × 2 = 0.500 ------- 0.500 × 2 = 1.000-------- 1 0.62510 = 0.1012 4', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 2027, 740, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00741', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'The Decimal value of the ASCII code of is 67. which ASCII values represent the characters and ?', '["1001111, 1010001", "1000011, 1000011", "1000010, 1000101", "1110011, 1100001", "1000011, 1000001"]'::jsonb, 3, 'In the ASCII encoding each character is assigned a unique numerical value. The ASCII value for is 67 in decimal. Since comes before in the its ASCII value is one which is 66', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 2027, 741, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00742', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'What is the primary function of a full adder in digital circuits?', '["To perform addition of two binary numbers with a carry-in input. carry-in wdodkhla", "To perform subtraction of two binary numbers", "To multiply two binary numbers", "To divide two binary numbers", "To compare two binary numbers"]'::jsonb, 1, 'The basic function of a full adder in digital circuits is to add two binary numbers with a carry-in input. In a full adder only addition takes place. All remaining calculations are done through addition. 2''s complements are also used for that. 5', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 2027, 742, '2027 Quiz Series'),
