('alict_00851', 5, 'Operating Systems & File Management', 'Which of the following best describes a directory in a file system?', '["A directory is a type of file that stores data in a structured format for easy retrieval", "A directory is a special file that contains information about other files and subdirectories", "A directory is used to manage system memory and allocate resources to processes", "A directory is a file that contains executable code to run applications", "A directory is a secure area of the file system where encrypted files are stored"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Option 1: According to this it is false. A directory itself does not store user data in a structured used to organize files. Option 2: According to this it is true', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Operating Systems & File Management', 2027, 851, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00852', 5, 'Operating Systems & File Management', 'In a File Allocation Table (FAT) what does the FAT table primarily store?', '["File names and their corresponding sizes", "User permissions for accessing files", "The location of the first cluster of each file", "Metadata about the file system itself", "A list of all available storage blocks"]'::jsonb, 3, 'The File Allocation Table (FAT) maintains a list of all the clusters allocated to specifically indicating the location of the first cluster of each file. This allows the operating system to locate and retrieve the data associated with a file by following the chain of clusters. wkq', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Operating Systems & File Management', 2027, 852, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00853', 5, 'Operating Systems & File Management', 'The size of each category (Block size) is 3KB. A portion of the disk''s file partition table looks like the tla (Block size) 3KB tu fldgila The last category of a file is indicated by wjika -1 u.ska Directory information related to a file indicates the category number of the first category of the file. f.dkqjlg olajhs'' m%udKh oelafjkafka o?', '["197, 9KB", "121, 12KB", "199, 12KB", "120, 3KB", "121, 16KB"]'::jsonb, 2, 'to find out how many blocks the file start with -1, which represents the last and get the corresponding block number. Then find if there is another block with that number. If that is the block number should be obtained as before', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Operating Systems & File Management', 2027, 853, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00854', 5, 'Operating Systems & File Management', 'Operating system generally used in a mobile phone is best described cx.u fyd¢ka lr o?', '["Real-time operating system", "Embedded operating system", "Multiuser operating system", "Single user multi tasking operating system", "Single tasking operating system"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Mobile phones typically use a single-user multitasking operating which allows a single user to run multiple applications simultaneously. This operating system is optimized for mobile devices to manage tasks such as phone internet and app usage efficiently', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Operating Systems & File Management', 2027, 854, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00855', 5, 'Operating Systems & File Management', 'What is the primary function of an operating system''s command interpreter?', '["Displaying graphics", "Executing hardware operations", "Interpreting and executing commands provided by the user", "Managing file storage", "Enhancing system security"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Option 1: According to this it''s false. Displaying graphics is typically managed by the graphical user interface (GUI) and the system''s display not the command interpreter. ,nkafka Option 2: According to this it''s false', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Operating Systems & File Management', 2027, 855, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00856', 5, 'Operating Systems & File Management', 'In memory which of the following statements is true regarding the relationship between virtual memory and physical memory?', '["Virtual memory is always smaller than physical memory", "Virtual memory can exceed physical memory capacity", "Physical memory is a subset of virtual memory", "Memory mapping does not involve the operating system", "Virtual memory and physical memory are the same"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Correct answer: "Virtual memory can exceed physical memory capacity". This reflects standard operating-system concepts (process/file/memory management) as usually taught at A/L.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Operating Systems & File Management', 2027, 856, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00857', 5, 'Operating Systems & File Management', 'If the main memory size is 8GB and the page size in virtual memory is how many bits are needed for the frame number of a physical memory address?', '["8 bits", "10 bits", "22 bits", "11 bits", "32 bits"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Correct answer: "11 bits". This reflects standard operating-system concepts (process/file/memory management) as usually taught at A/L.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Operating Systems & File Management', 2027, 857, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00858', 5, 'Operating Systems & File Management', 'A process is interrupted because its allocated time for execution has expired. What is the correct state transition?', '["Running \u2192 Blocked", "Running \u2192 Ready", "Ready \u2192 Running", "Blocked \u2192 Ready", "Ready \u2192 Blocked"]'::jsonb, 2, 'A process is interrupted because its time slice has expired. This is typical when each process is given a limited amount of time to use the CPU. When that time runs the CPU stops the and the process is moved back to the Ready state so that other processes can get a turn', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Operating Systems & File Management', 2027, 858, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00859', 5, 'Operating Systems & File Management', 'Which of the following is a major difference between the FAT32 and file systems?', '["FAT32 supports file while does not. FAT32", "has a file size limit of 4 but FAT32 can store larger files. 4 GB", "FAT32 is compatible with more operating while offers better security features. FAT32", "cannot recover from disk but FAT32 can. yg", "FAT32 is more secure than due to its advanced permissions system. FAT32 tys Wiia wjir"]'::jsonb, 3, 'FAT32 is an older file system and works on a wide variety of devices and operating systems. it has a 4 GB file size limit and lacks advanced features. FAT32 is a more modern file system with advanced security including file encryption and detailed permissions', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Operating Systems & File Management', 2027, 859, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00860', 5, 'Operating Systems & File Management', 'Which of the following is a key feature of the file system?', '["It does not support file compression", "It allows for file permissions and security attributes. th wjir", "It has a maximum file size limit of 2 GB", "It is primarily used in UNIX-based operating systems. th", "It does not support journaling"]'::jsonb, 2, '(New Technology File System) includes advanced features such as support for file permissions and security allowing for better data protection and access control compared to older file systems. 5', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Operating Systems & File Management', 2027, 860, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00861', 5, 'Operating Systems & File Management', 'When a new process is which of the following happens first?', '["The process receives I", "The process is allocated memory for its execution", "The process starts executing its instructions", "The operating system loads executable code into memory", "The process is assigned a Process ID (PID)"]'::jsonb, 5, 'The typical sequence of process creation is as 1) Assign PID OS assigns a unique identifier to the process. 2) Memory allocation Space is given in RAM for the process. 3) Loading the code The OS loads executable instructions into memory', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Operating Systems & File Management', 2027, 861, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00862', 5, 'Operating Systems & File Management', 'Which of the statements is correct regarding schedulers?', '["Short term scheduler is used to swap the process between memories", "Long term scheduler sends the selected processes from the ready state processes through dispatch", "Short term scheduler is faster than other two schedulers", "Long term scheduler speed is seen as the speed between the other two schedulers", "Midterm scheduler loads the selected processes to execute into memory from portion of the processes"]'::jsonb, 3, '• Option 1: This statement is incorrect. The short -term also known as the CPU selects which ready process in memory should be allocated the CPU next. Swapping processes between memory and secondary storage is typically handled by the medium-term scheduler', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Operating Systems & File Management', 2027, 862, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00863', 5, 'Operating Systems & File Management', 'It represents a temporary halt in the process execution while waiting for necessary events or resources tobecome available. wjYH ,efnk th lrhs'' Which state of the process transition does apply to the above statement?', '["Ready state", "Running state", "Swapped and Ready state", "Swapped and Blocked state", "Blocked state"]'::jsonb, 5, 'Ready State The process is ready to run but waiting for CPU allocation. CPU fjka 2) Running State The process is actively executing on the CPU. 3) Swapped and Ready State The process is ready to run but swapped out to secondary storage', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Operating Systems & File Management', 2027, 863, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00864', 5, 'Operating Systems & File Management', 'Which memory management technique divides memory into fixed-size blocks?', '["Paging", "Segmentation", "Contiguous allocation", "Swapping", "Dynamic partitioning"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Option 1: Paging divides memory into fixed-size blocks called pages and maps them to frames in physical memory. Option 2: Segmentation divides memory into variable-sized segments. Option 3: Contiguous allocation requires adjacent memory unlike paging', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Operating Systems & File Management', 2027, 864, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00865', 5, 'Operating Systems & File Management', 'In a memory management a page fault occurs when a program tries to access a page that is not currently in physical memory. Which component of the operating system is responsible for handling page faults and bringing the required page into memory?', '["Device Driver", "Scheduler", "File System Manager", "Memory Management Unit (MMU)", "Network Protocol Stack"]'::jsonb, 4, 'While the MMU is a hardware it works in close conjunction with the operating system''s memory management policies. When a page fault the MMU traps this event and signals the operating system', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Operating Systems & File Management', 2027, 865, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00866', 5, 'Operating Systems & File Management', 'Which of the following is not a function of the Operating System?', '["Memory management", "File system management", "Compiler design", "Process scheduling", "Device management"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Memory Management The OS allocates and deallocates memory space as needed by programs. u.ska It tracks memory usage and handles and segmentation. th File System Management OS provides structure for and organizing files on storage devices', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Operating Systems & File Management', 2027, 866, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00867', 5, 'Operating Systems & File Management', 'Which of the following transitions is not valid in the seven-state process model?', '["Running \u2192 Blocked", "Swapped out and ready\u2192 Running", "Ready \u2192 Running", "New \u2192 Ready", "Blocked \u2192 Ready"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Option 1: This occurs when a process in execution needs to wait for an I to the waiting (blocked) state. I Option 2: This transition skips the "Ready" state', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Operating Systems & File Management', 2027, 867, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00868', 5, 'Operating Systems & File Management', 'A file is stored on a disk using the FAT file system. The file starts at block 4, and FAT table looks like f.dkqjla lr 4ka FAT wdldrfhka fmfka( What is the sequence of blocks that make up the file?', '["4, 5, 10", "4, 7, 10", "4, 7, 9", "4, 10, 7", "4, 6, 7"]'::jsonb, 2, 'In a FAT file each entry in the FAT table points to the next block of the file. According to the block 4 points to block 7, and block 7 points to block 10. FAT 4 u.ska 7 o" 7 u', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Operating Systems & File Management', 2027, 868, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00869', 5, 'Operating Systems & File Management', 'Which of the following is not included in a PCB?', '["Process state", "Pointer", "Process ID", "Program counter", "System logs"]'::jsonb, 5, 'A Process Control Block (PCB) is a data structure used by the operating system to store important information about a process. Contains all the details the operating system needs to manage and track processes during execution', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Operating Systems & File Management', 2027, 869, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00870', 5, 'Operating Systems & File Management', 'A process running on the system logs the following igyka lrhs( "Execution time limit Process will blaujd wjika jkq component enforces this termination?', '["The process scheduler", "The memory manager", "The interrupt handler", "The file system manager", "The device manager"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Option 1: Correct. Manages process execution and enforces time terminating processes that exceed their allocated time. Option 2: Incorrect. Handles memory allocation and unrelated to time limits. Option 3: Incorrect', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Operating Systems & File Management', 2027, 870, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00871', 5, 'Operating Systems & File Management', 'Which of the following is false regarding paging in memory management?', '["A page table is used to map logical addresses to physical addresses", "Paging can result in internal fragmentation", "Logical memory is divided into blocks of the same size called pages", "Frames are not equal sized", "Paging allows the logical address space of a process to be non-contiguous"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Paging is a memory management technique used by operating systems to manage and utilize physical memory more efficiently. It divides the process''s logical address space into fixed-size blocks called and divides the physical memory into fixed-size blocks called frames', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Operating Systems & File Management', 2027, 871, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00872', 5, 'Operating Systems & File Management', 'What is the primary function of resource management in an operating system?', '["Ensuring data is encrypted", "Allocating hardware and software resources to", "Updating system", "Managing network", "Optimizing system"]'::jsonb, 2, 'The primary function of resource management in an operating system is allocating hardware and software resources to applications. This includes managing CPU and input to ensure that different applications and processes have the necessary resources to function properly', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Operating Systems & File Management', 2027, 872, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00873', 5, 'Operating Systems & File Management', 'What can be a potential disadvantage of frequent swapping?', '["Faster process", "Increased system security", "Decreased system performance due to higher disk I", "Lower memory utilization", "Reduced number of running processes"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Swapping is a process in operating systems where inactive programs or parts of programs are temporarily moved from the main memory (RAM) to a virtual memory to free up memory for other active programs', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Operating Systems & File Management', 2027, 873, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00874', 5, 'Operating Systems & File Management', 'What is the purpose of process termination in operating systems?', '["Releasing resources allocated to the process", "Saving the process state for future use", "Switching the process to a blocked state", "Suspending the process temporarily", "Allocating additional memory to the process"]'::jsonb, 1, 'The purpose of process termination in operating systems is to release the resources that were allocated to the process during its execution', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Operating Systems & File Management', 2027, 874, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00875', 5, 'Operating Systems & File Management', 'What is the function of the Master File Table (MFT) in', '["It keeps track of disk partitions. th", "It stores a list of all file attributes and locations on the disk. th", "It monitors user access permissions. th", "It maintains the directory structure of the file system. th", "It converts file formats for compatibility. th"]'::jsonb, 2, 'The Master File Table (MFT) in primarily functions to store a list of all file attributes and their locations on the as described in Option 2', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Operating Systems & File Management', 2027, 875, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00876', 5, 'Operating Systems & File Management', 'What type of data structure does the operating system use for each process running on the computer?', '["Offset fkrej", "Page", "Page Number", "Page Table", "Virtual Memory"]'::jsonb, 4, 'In an operating a page table is a data structure used to manage virtual memory for each running process. It maps virtual memory addresses used by a program to physical memory addresses in the computer''s RAM', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Operating Systems & File Management', 2027, 876, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00877', 5, 'Operating Systems & File Management', 'Which of the following is NOT a feature of a real-time operating system (RTOS)?', '["Deterministic response time", "Efficient memory management", "Support for multitasking", "Dynamic memory allocation for critical processes", "Guaranteed timing constraints"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Option 1: Real-time operating systems ensure predictable response times for critical making this a core feature. Option 2: RTOSs typically include efficient memory management to minimize overhead and ensure predictable performance. RTOS', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Operating Systems & File Management', 2027, 877, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00878', 5, 'Operating Systems & File Management', 'In a time-shared operating system using Round Robin which factor most critically affects the system''s responsiveness?', '["The number of processes in the ready queue", "The process burst time", "The size of the time quantum", "The I", "The process priority level"]'::jsonb, 3, 'In a time-shared operating Round Robin (RR) scheduling is one of the most common algorithms used to allocate CPU time fairly among all processes', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Operating Systems & File Management', 2027, 878, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00879', 5, 'Operating Systems & File Management', 'The block size of a disk is 4KB. A portion of its File Allocation Table (FAT) at a particular time is shown below. The portion shown indicates the blocks of the data.bin file as fldgil 4KB tys fldgila fmkajd fldgfia data.bin fldgia o The last block of a file is indicated by -1', '["120, 12KB", "120, 16KB", "121, 12KB", "121, 16KB", "122, 8KB"]'::jsonb, 1, 'To answer this let''s analyze the given information and FAT entries to determine the directory entry (first block) and the disk space allocated for the data.bin file. m%Yakhg fjka lr Analyzing the FAT and blocks used We are given that • Last block of a file is indicated by -1', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Operating Systems & File Management', 2027, 879, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00880', 6, 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', 'Among the following data which one is immutable in Python?', '["List", "Dictionary", "Set", "Tuple", "List and Set"]'::jsonb, 4, '• List A list is meaning you can modify its elements after it''s created. For you can add or remove items', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', 2027, 880, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00881', 6, 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', 'Which of the followings is correct with respect to big data?', '["High volume is one of the features of big data. uyd", "Big data is always structured. uyd", "Data generated through social media such as Facebook cannot be considered as big data. Facebook jeks iudc", "A Management Information System (MIS) is always required to collect big", "Python is not a suitable programming language to manage big data"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Option 1: This statement correctly identifies one of the key features of big which is the large volume of data. Big data involves dealing with massive amounts of data that traditional data processing systems may find challenging to handle efficiently', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', 2027, 881, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00882', 6, 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', 'What is the characteristic of quality information that shows in the "A student achieving highest marks for ICT in a term test is not sufficient to decide his rank in his class"?', '["Relevancy", "Timeliness", "Low cost", "Accuracy", "Completeness"]'::jsonb, 5, 'The characteristic of quality information reflected in the "A student achieving highest marks for ICT in a term test is not sufficient to decide his rank in his is Completeness. "jdr Let''s go through the given options', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', 2027, 882, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00883', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'A computer port is used to?', '["Communicate with hard disks", "Download files", "Communicate with other computer peripherals", "Delete files uelsug", "None of the above"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Correct answer: "Communicate with other computer peripherals". This reflects how this hardware component/device is defined and used in a standard computer system.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', NULL, 883, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_00884', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of the following is both input and an output device?', '["Monitor", "Mouse", "Speaker", "Touchscreen", "Keyboard"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Correct answer: "Monitor". This reflects how this hardware component/device is defined and used in a standard computer system.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', NULL, 884, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_00885', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of the following early computers is often credited as the first to implement the concept of a stored- program architecture?', '["ENIAC (Electronic Numerical Integrator and Computer): ENIAC was one of the earliest but it did not initially use a stored-program architecture. It was programmed using external switches and plugboards. ENIAC", "UNIV AC I (Universal Automatic Computer I): UNIV AC I was one of the first commercially available computers and did use a stored -program but it came after the Manchester Baby. UNIV AC I", "EDV AC (Electronic Discrete Variable Automatic Computer): EDV AC was designed to use a stored-program architecture and had significant theoretical contributions from John von Neumann. it was not the first to become operational. EDV AC", "Manchester Baby is also known as the Small-Scale Experimental Machine (SSEM), was the first computer to successfully run a program stored in its which is the essence of the stored -program architecture. This machine was operational in 1948 and was designed at the University of Manchester. Manchester Baby", "ENIAC"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Correct answer: "ENIAC (Electronic Numerical Integrator and Computer): ENIAC was one of the earliest but it did not initially use a stored-program architecture. It was programmed using external switches and plugboards. ENIAC". This reflects how this hardware component/device is defined and used in a standard computer system.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', NULL, 885, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_00886', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'The stored programme concept was presented by..?', '["John von Neumann Introduced the stored -program where both data and programs are stored in a computer''s forming the basis of most modern computer architectures. fndfyda .Dy", "Ada Lovelace Recognized as the world''s first computer programmer for her work on Charles Babbage''s Analytical she conceptualized algorithms to be executed by a machine. Charles Babbage''s Analytical Engine", "John Eckert Co-inventor of the one of the earliest general -purpose electronic digital but not directly associated with the stored-program concept. ENIAC", "Charles Babbage Known as the \"father of the he designed the Analytical a mechanical general - purpose but did not develop the stored-program concept", "Blaise Pascal Invented one of the earliest mechanical the but did not contribute to the concept of stored programs in computing"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Correct answer: "John von Neumann Introduced the stored -program where both data and programs are stored in a computer''s forming the basis of most modern computer architectures. fndfyda .Dy". This reflects how this hardware component/device is defined and used in a standard computer system.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', NULL, 886, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_00887', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of the following devices would most likely be used for high-resolution color printing?', '["Inkjet printer", "Laser printer", "Dot matrix printer", "Thermal printer", "D printer"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Correct answer: "Inkjet printer". This reflects how this hardware component/device is defined and used in a standard computer system.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', NULL, 887, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_00888', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of the following is NOT a type of cache fkdjkafka : 4) Explanation', '["L1 cache", "L2 cache", "L3 cache", "L4 cache", "None of the above"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Correct answer: "L1 cache". This reflects how this hardware component/device is defined and used in a standard computer system.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', NULL, 888, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_00889', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of the following is an example of a CPU socket type?', '["USB-C This statement is false. USB-C is a type of connector used for data and video output. It is not related to CPU socket which are specific to mounting processors on a motherboard", "HDMI This statement is false. HDMI (High -Definition Multimedia Interface) is a standard for transmitting audio and video signals between such as from a computer to a monitor or TV . It is not associated with CPU sockets", "LGA 1151 This statement is true. LGA 1151 is a CPU socket type used by Intel processors. The term \"LGA\" stands for Land Grid which refers to the physical layout of pins on the socket that make contact with the CPU. LGA 1151 is one of the many socket types designed to fit specific generations of Intel processors", "DDR4 This statement is false. DDR4 (Double Data Rate", "is a type of RAM (Random Access Memory) used in computers. It refers to a memory not a CPU socket type"]'::jsonb, 1, 'USB - C 2) HDMI 3) LGA 1151 4) DDR4 5) SATA', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', NULL, 889, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
