VALUES
('alict_00901', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of the following components is directly connected to the Southbridge chip in a traditional computer architecture?', '["RAM", "USB ports", "Processor", "None of the above", "PCIe slots"]'::jsonb, 4, 'In a traditional computer architecture with a Northbridge-Southbridge the Southbridge is responsible for managing lower-speed peripheral while the Northbridge handles high-speed components like RAM and the CPU. Northbridge-Southbridge tlla jeks', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', NULL, 901, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_00902', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'In which generation of computers began the use of integrated circuits of ultra large scale?', '["First computer generation", "Second computer generation", "Third computer generation", "Fourth computer generation", "Fifth computer generation"]'::jsonb, 5, 'First computer generation - Vacuum tubes Second computer generation - Transistor fojk Third computer generation - Integrated Circuits Fourth computer generation - Large scale integrated circuits Fifth computer generation - Ultra large scale integrated circuits miajk', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', NULL, 902, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_00903', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which type of memory is volatile and loses its contents when power is turned tys 1) Volatile Memory', '["RAM", "ROM", "Hard Drive", "SSD", "Flash Memory 3"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Correct answer: "RAM". This reflects how this hardware component/device is defined and used in a standard computer system.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', NULL, 903, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_00904', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'State the technology that was removed at the beginning of the third generation', '["Vacuum tube", "Transistor g%dkaisiagr", "Integrated circuit", "Microprocessor ilik", "Microchips"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Option 1: The third generation of computers (1960s-1970s) saw the replacement of vacuum tubes with transistors and integrated circuits (ICs). First-generation computers used vacuum which were and produced a lot of heat', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', NULL, 904, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_00905', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of the following is NOT a characteristic of RAM?', '["V olatile memory", "Faster than hard drives", "Stores data permanently", "Used for temporary storage", "Directly accessible by the CPU"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Option 1: Correct. RAM (Random Access Memory) is a volatile meaning it loses its data when the power is turned off. Option 2: Correct. It is used for temporary storage of data that the CPU needs to access quickly. it is much faster than hard drives. Option 3: Incorrect', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', NULL, 905, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_00906', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'What is the role of a spindle in a hard disk?', '["Holds and moves the head to places", "Holds the platter firmly and spins it", "Exchanges data in and out of the HDD", "Controls the speed of data transfer", "Converts digital data into magnetic signals"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Option 1: Incorrect. The actuator arm moves the read Option 2: Correct. The spindle holds the platters in place and rotates them at high speeds. Some have speeds of 5400 RPM or 7200 RPM. RPM 7200 RPM Option 3: Incorrect', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', NULL, 906, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_00907', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of the following isn''t a main part of the CPU?', '["Arithmetic Logical Unit", "Control Unit", "Cache", "Memory Unit", "Registers"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Option 1: Correct. The ALU performs all arithmetic etc.) and logical operations etc.). It is a core component of the CPU. NOT Option 2: Correct. The control unit directs the flow of instructions and manages execution within the CPU', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', NULL, 907, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_00908', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'What is the primary function of the CPU?', '["Store data", "Process instructions", "Display output", "Connect to the internet", "Provide power to the system"]'::jsonb, 2, 'The CPU is responsible for interpreting and executing instructions from programs and the operating system. It carries out operations such as logical and data manipulation based on the instructions it receives', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', NULL, 908, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_00909', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Ethernet The Ethernet port is used for wired network allowing devices to connect to local area networks (LANs) and the internet. This port is not designed for video output is not used to connect monitors or whether old or new. Ethernet', '["USB", "HDMI", "Display port", "Ethernet", "VGA 5. VGA The Video Graphics Array (VGA) port is an analog interface that has been widely used for many years to connect older monitors and projectors. VGA transmits video signals and is compatible with many older display making it the correct port for connecting older monitors and projectors. Video Graphics Array (VGA)"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Correct answer: "USB". This reflects how this hardware component/device is defined and used in a standard computer system.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', NULL, 909, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_00910', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of the following memory devices has the lowest memory capacity?', '["USB flash drive", "Dynamic Random Access Memory", "Cache memory", "Registers", "Read Only Memory"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Among the options registers typically have the lowest memory capacity. They are high- speed storage locations within the CPU designed to hold data temporarily during processing. They are used to store data that are being currently processed or frequently accessed instructions', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', NULL, 910, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_00911', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which input initially developed for use with flight gained popularity in the 1980s as a gaming controller and alternative pointing device for ixj¾Okh ,o gaming controlors 3) Explanation of each option', '["Trackball", "Light pen", "Joystick", "Touchpad", "Graphics tablet 2"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Correct answer: "Trackball". This reflects how this hardware component/device is defined and used in a standard computer system.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', NULL, 911, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_00912', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'What is one of the most commonly used keyboard designed in the 1870s? 1870 jq mqjre 1) Explanation of each option', '["QWERTY", "DVORAK", "COLEMAK", "AZERTY", "ANSI Option"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Correct answer: "QWERTY". This reflects how this hardware component/device is defined and used in a standard computer system.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', NULL, 912, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_00913', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of the following port transmit video as analog ;rx. j¾.h 4) Explanation of each option', '["Display port", "DVI", "HDMI", "RCA connector", "USB Type-C Option"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Correct answer: "RCA connector". This reflects how this hardware component/device is defined and used in a standard computer system.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', NULL, 913, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_00914', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Floppy Disks (E) Floppy disks do not utilize flash memory. They use magnetic storage technology similar to external hard disk which involves magnetic fields to store and retrieve Tjqka Odjlhkag iudk ,nd the correct answer is 5) and Communication ;dlaIKh 2026', '["A only", "B only", "D only", "C and E only", "A and D only A B D C E A D 2"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Correct answer: "A only". This reflects how this hardware component/device is defined and used in a standard computer system.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', NULL, 914, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_00915', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'What is the purpose of the Control Unit in V on Neumann architecture?', '["Performing arithmetic and logical operations. wxl", "Generating graphical outputs to the monitor", "Managing input", "Storing temporary data for quick access. blauka", "Coordinating communication between different nodes"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Option 1: Performing arithmetic and logical operations is the function of the Arithmetic Logic Unit (ALU), not the Control Unit. wxl Option 2: Graphical output is handled by the GPU (Graphics Processing Unit) or display not the CU', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', NULL, 915, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_00916', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'What type of CPU has the small connector trays on the processor and the pins on the motherboard? ilikh CPU j¾.h 1) Explanation', '["LGA", "PGA", "BGA", "NGA", "FGA 2. E1216 - 11308 = ..................... What will be the answer for above calculation?"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Converting E1216 & 11308 into decimal E1216 E (14) 1 2 162 161 160 256 × 14 16 × 1 × 2 3584 + 16 + 2 360210 Calculation = 360210 - 60010 = 300210 Converting decimal to binary 300210 211 210 29 28 27 26 25 24 23 22 21 20 1 0 1 0 1 0 1 0 1011101110102 Converting binary to octal 1011101110102', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', NULL, 916, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_00917', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'What type of memory is known as an empty memory unit which was introduced in 1970 and the stored data cannot be changed or deleted after the program is executed? 1970 ysia .; miq lr uld fkdyels j¾.h o? Answer : 3 ) Explanation of each option', '["EPRAM", "EEPROM", "PROM", "EPROM", "Flash ROM"]'::jsonb, 3, 'BCD (Binary-Coded Decimal) is a representation of decimal digits (0-9) using 4-bit binary numbers. Each 4-bit group in a BCD value must range from 0000 (decimal 0) to 1001 (decimal 9) to be valid. If any 4 - bit group exceeds this the entire value becomes invalid', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', NULL, 917, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_00918', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', '000110112 + E416 - 5 = 4) Explanation', '["Cache", "Clipboard", "Buffer", "Memory Stick", "Swap Space"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Let''s simplify the given Boolean expression. ,nd = A. B. C̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅ + (A + B̅)̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅ = (A. B. C̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅). (A + B̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅) De Morgan''s law = A. B. C. (A + B̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅) Double inverse law = A. B. C. A̅. B̿ De Morgan''s law = A. B. C. A̅. B Double inverse law = A. A̅. B. B', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', NULL, 918, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_00919', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'What is the main advantage of magnetic Hard Disk Drives (HDD) over Solid State Drives (SSD)?', '["Higher data transfer rates", "Lower power consumption", "Lower heat generation", "Lower cost per gigabyte", "Compatibility with a wider range of devices"]'::jsonb, 4, 'The main advantage of magnetic Hard Disk Drives (HDD) over Solid State Drives (SSD) is their lower cost per gigabyte. use more established technology and can store large amounts of data at a relatively lower price compared to', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', NULL, 919, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_00920', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of the following storage types offers the fastest access time?', '["Hard disk drive", "Solid State Drive (SSD)", "Read-Only Memory (ROM)", "Random Access Memory (RAM)", "Magnetic Tape"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Option 1: Relatively slow due to mechanical parts (spinning read fldgia Option 2: Much faster than as it uses flash memory and has no moving but still slower than RAM', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', NULL, 920, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_00921', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of the following scanning devices is the most suitable to check multiple-choice answer sheets : 4) Let''s take a look at each device', '["MICR Reads characters printed with magnetic typically found on checks. It processes and verifies documents like checks by reading magnetic ink ensuring that they are authentic and legible", "OCR Converts different types of such as scanned paper documents or into editable data. It scans and recognizes printed or handwritten allowing the content to be edited or processed digitally. ,o lvodis", "Barcode Reader", "OMR Specifically used for reading marks made on such as bubbles filled in on multiple -choice tests or surveys. It detects the presence of marks in specific locations on a making it ideal for grading exams or processing survey responses", "Flatbed Scanner Scans or other flat items into a digital format. It captures an image of the document or photo placed on its glass surface and converts it into a digital often used for general document scanning"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Correct answer: "MICR Reads characters printed with magnetic typically found on checks. It processes and verifies documents like checks by reading magnetic ink ensuring that they are authentic and legible". This reflects how this hardware component/device is defined and used in a standard computer system.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', NULL, 921, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_00922', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of the following best describes an integrated circuit (IC)?', '["A semiconductor device that contains multiple electronic such as transistors and on a single chip", "A single resistor that can be used in various electronic circuits", "A type of circuit board used to mount and connect various electronic components", "A standalone device that performs a single such as amplifying a signal. ix{djla", "A passive electronic component used to store electrical energy temporarily"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Correct answer: "A semiconductor device that contains multiple electronic such as transistors and on a single chip". This reflects how this hardware component/device is defined and used in a standard computer system.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', NULL, 922, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_00923', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which computer had the world''s first graphical user 3) Let''s go through the given options', '["Apple II (1977) A popular early personal computer from but it used a command -line interface rather than a GUI. Apple", "IBM 704 (1954) An early mainframe computer that used punched cards and had no GUI", "Apple Macintosh Released in 1984, the Apple Macintosh was the first commercially successful computer to popularize the GUI concept to a broad audience. It built on ideas from the Xerox Alto but made them accessible to consumers. The Macintosh included a mouse and a user-friendly interface with icons and which revolutionized personal computing. 1984", "UNIV AC 1108 (1964) Part of the UNIV AC series of also lacking a GUI. UNIV AC m%Odk fldgils\" GUI tlla o", "CDC 3600 (1964) A mainframe computer from Control Data again without a GUI. GUI"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Since all the numbers are given in base 8, we can perform the calculation directly. 778 + 118 = 1108 - 348 = 548 the answer of the above calculation is 54 8. But the answers are given in binary form. we have to convert 548 to binary form to get the answer', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', NULL, 923, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_00924', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Central Processing Unit controls the other devices and performs the arithmetical operations while ............ is a specialized processor which manages the memory and displays the images on the monitor. This is also used in parallel personal work stations and game consoles. Which is the most suitable word for the blank ?', '["Graphic Processing Unit", "Control Unit", "Arithmetic Logic Unit", "Buffer", "Virtual Memory"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Correct answer: "Graphic Processing Unit". This reflects how this hardware component/device is defined and used in a standard computer system.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', NULL, 924, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_00925', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Computer technology has advanced leading to the development of more compact and efficient devices. Which of the following innovation played a crucial role in increasing the speed of computers?', '["Magnetic Drum", "Transistors", "Magnetic Tape", "Punched Cards", "Mechanical Relays"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Correct answer: "Transistors". This reflects how this hardware component/device is defined and used in a standard computer system.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', NULL, 925, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_00926', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'The invention of the "3 pin vacuum tube", laid the foundation for the modern computer technology. The person who is honored for this is ?', '["John Presper Eckert", "Lee De Forest", "John V Atanasoff", "Gottfried Wilhelm", "Howard Aiken"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Lee De Forest is credited with the invention of the vacuum tube (also known as the electronic valve)', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', NULL, 926, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_00927', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of the following input devices is used to check the validity of a cheque?', '["Magnetic stripe reader", "Smart card reader", "Magnetic ink character reader", "Flatbed Scanner", "Optical mark recognition"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Magnetic stripe reader This device is used to read the magnetic stripe on credit debit and other similar cards. It is not used for cheques. Kh th 2) Smart card reader This device reads smart which have an embedded microchip', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', NULL, 927, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_00928', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which statement about early computing machines is incorrect?', '["ENIAC was the first general-purpose electronic digital computer. ENIAC", "The abacus was used before the invention of mechanical calculators", "The Jacquard loom used punched cards to control weaving patterns", "Honeywell series computers belong to the second generation of computers. Honeywell series fojk", "Vacuum tubes were widely used before transistors. g%dkaisiagr"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Option 1: This is correct. ENIAC (Electronic Numerical Integrator and Computer) was the first general- purpose digital computer. It could be programmed to perform complex sequences of operations and marked a major advancement in computing', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', NULL, 928, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_00929', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'The statement that best describes the result of fragmentation on a hard disk', '["Some files are deleted from the hard drive. iuyr", "The data access speed of the hard disk is reduced", "The hard disk is not distributed on a local area network", "The number of bad sectors increases", "An existing file is removed and another file is placed"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Fragmentation occurs when files are broken up into pieces and stored in different parts of the hard disk. This happens over time as files are and deleted. As a the hard disk has to work harder to read these scattered file which reduces the data access speed', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', NULL, 929, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_00930', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which device cannot be categorized under both input and output devices?', '["MICR", "Headsets", "Electronic whiteboard", "Network Cards", "Modems"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Correct answer: "Network Cards". This reflects how this hardware component/device is defined and used in a standard computer system.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', NULL, 930, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_00931', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of the following statements about the history of computing is correct?', '["ENIAC - First transistor-based general-purpose computer ENIAC -", "Jacquard Loom - Introduced punched cards for automation", "IBM 1401 - First mechanical calculator used in education IBM 1401 -", "Pascaline - First programmable mechanical computer", "UNIV AC I - First computer to use vacuum tubes UNIV AC I -"]'::jsonb, 1, '• Option 1: ENIAC was a electronic computer built in the 1940s that used thousands of vacuum tubes to perform calculations. it was not tubes in computers for better efficiency and reliability. ENIAC g%dkaisiagr miqj fidhd .kakd ,o', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', NULL, 931, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_00932', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which output device produces a hard copy output by spraying tiny ink droplets onto paper?', '["Laser printer", "Dot matrix printer", "Thermal printer", "Inkjet printer", "D printer Answer"]'::jsonb, 1, 'An inkjet printer works by propelling very small droplets of liquid ink directly onto paper to create an image or text. It is known for its ability to produce high-quality color prints and is commonly used for home and office printing', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', NULL, 932, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_00933', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'What is the purpose of the spindle in a hard disk?', '["Moving the actuator arm", "Storing data", "Rotating the platters", "data", "Managing data transfer"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Correct answer: "Rotating the platters". This reflects how this hardware component/device is defined and used in a standard computer system.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', NULL, 933, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_00934', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'An output device that creates a hard copy by precisely spraying tiny droplets of ink onto paper is known as a', '["Laser printer", "Dot matrix printer", "Thermal printer", "Inkjet printer", "D printer"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Laser printers use a laser beam to create an electrostatic image on a which then attracts toner (a dry powder) that is fused onto the paper with heat. Dot matrix printers use an impact where a print head with a series of pins strikes an ink- soaked ribbon against the paper', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', NULL, 934, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_00935', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'What is the Main function of the ALU?', '["Execute operating system commands", "Perform arithmetic and logical operations", "Control system performance", "Allocate memory space", "Manage network connections"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Correct answer: "Perform arithmetic and logical operations". This reflects how this hardware component/device is defined and used in a standard computer system.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', NULL, 935, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_00936', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'What is the primary purpose of a USB (Universal Serial Bus) port?', '["To provide power to the CPU", "To connect the CPU to the motherboard", "To connect storage devices like hard drives", "To connect a wide variety of peripheral devices to a computer", "To establish network connections between computers"]'::jsonb, 4, 'The "Universal" part of the name is key. It was designed to standardize the connection of many different types of devices', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', NULL, 936, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_00937', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'What is the primary purpose of an arithmetic logic unit (ALU) in a CPU?', '["To store data permanently", "To control the flow of instructions", "To perform arithmetic and logical operations", "To connect peripheral devices", "To manage the computer''s memory"]'::jsonb, 3, 'ALU stands for Arithmetic Logic Unit. The name itself explains its function. ALU Arithmetic operations include and division', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', NULL, 937, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_00938', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Consider the following and flash (solid state) memories are different types of secondary storage used to store data and hkq j¾.fha Magnetic such as hard disk drives and use magnetic fields to magnetize tiny individual sections of a metal spinning Odjl jeks lerflk fldgia Optical devices such as and Blu -ray discs use a laser to scan the surface of a spinning disc made from metal and plastic. CD" DVD Blu-ray jeks idok ,o lerflk 5) Explanation of each statement', '["A only", "B only", "C only", "A and B only", "All of the above A B C A B"]'::jsonb, 2, 'When the above 3 numbers are converted into decimal it is clear that the decimal of only 2 numbers A and C is equal to 17910. 17910 g', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', NULL, 938, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_00939', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of the following memory types is volatile and directly accessible by the CPU during execution?', '["ROM", "EEPROM", "Cache Memory", "Virtual Memory", "Flash Memory"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Cache memory loses its data when the power is turned off. The CPU uses cache memory to store frequently accessed data and as it''s much faster than main memory (RAM). This direct and rapid access is crucial for improving system performance', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', NULL, 939, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_00940', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of the following is considered the first generation of computers?', '["Computers using Integrated Circuits (ICs)", "Computers using Vacuum Tubes", "Computers using Microprocessors", "Computers using Transistors", "Computers using Artificial Intelligence (AI) chips"]'::jsonb, 2, 'The first generation of computers (1940s-1950s) used vacuum tubes for circuitry and magnetic drums for memory. fnr These computers were and generated a lot of heat. Examples include the ENIAC and UNIV AC. ENIAC UNIV AC', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', NULL, 940, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_00941', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of the following(s) uses random access? wyUq lrkafka o@ A. Magnetic tape USB drive DVD 3) Explanation', '["A only. A", "A and B only. A B", "B and C only. B C", "All of the above", "None of the above"]'::jsonb, 5, 'let''s convert 4A616 into decimal. 4A616 4 A = 10 6 4 × 256 = 1024 10 × 16 = 160 6 × 1 1024 + 160 + 6 = 1190 4A616 = 119010 1190 + 99 = 1289 let''s convert the above answer back to hexadecimal', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', NULL, 941, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_00942', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of the following is located outside the Microprocessor?', '["ALU", "Regiseters", "RAM", "Level 1 Cache Memory", "Control Unit"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Correct answer: "RAM". This reflects how this hardware component/device is defined and used in a standard computer system.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', NULL, 942, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_00943', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of the following printers is used to print on fabric?', '["Laser printer", "D printer", "Offset printer", "Dye sublimation printer", "Inkjet printer"]'::jsonb, 4, 'The dye sublimation printer The dye sublimation printer is chosen because it is used specifically for printing on fabric. The dye is transferred onto the fabric using resulting in prints that are vibrant and durable', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', NULL, 943, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_00944', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'In 1904, the two-element vacuum tube was introduced 1904', '["John Ambrose Fleming", "Lee De Forest", "Howard Aiken", "Joseph Jacquard", "John von Neumann"]'::jsonb, 1, '• In 1904, John Ambrose Fleming introduced the double-ended vacuum tube. 1904 • In 1906, Lee de Frost improved upon it and made the three-terminal vacuum and this discovery marked the beginning of the subject of electronics', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', NULL, 944, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_00945', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which type of printer do the above characteristics belong j¾.hg o@ • Ink is stored in liquid form in tanks or cartridges and when printing ink is sprayed using gexls ,nhs'' • Colour accuracy and quality are high but the cost is high. j¾K ks 4) Explanation', '["Laser printer A laser printer is a type of printer that uses a laser beam to produce high -quality text and graphics by transferring toner (a powdered ink) onto paper. The laser creates an electrostatic image on a rotating which then attracts and transfers the tone r to the paper before it is fused with heat to create a permanent image. Laser printers are known for their and cost-effectiveness for high-volume printing", "Thermal printer A thermal printer is a type of printer that uses heat to produce images on special heat-sensitive paper. There are two main direct thermal which apply heat directly to the paper to create an and thermal transfer which use heat to transfer ink from a ribbon onto the paper. Thermal printers are commonly used for printing and barcodes due to their speed and efficiency", "Laser printer", "Thermal printer", "D printer"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Correct answer: "Laser printer A laser printer is a type of printer that uses a laser beam to produce high -quality text and graphics by transferring toner (a powdered ink) onto paper. The laser creates an electrostatic image on a rotating which then attracts and transfers the tone r to the paper before it is fused with heat to create a permanent image. Laser printers are known for their and cost-effectiveness for high-volume printing". This reflects how this hardware component/device is defined and used in a standard computer system.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', NULL, 945, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_00946', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which is the correct order from fastest access speed to slowest?', '["Cache > RAM > SSD > Optical disc", "RAM > Cache > SSD > Optical disc", "Cache > SSD > Optical disc > RAM", "SSD > Cache > RAM > Optical disc", "Cache > RAM > Optical disc > SSD"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Cache (Fastest) Cache memory is a high-speed memory located inside the CPU. It stores frequently used instructions and data to reduce CPU access time. RAM (Random Access Memory) RAM is much larger than cache and stores data temporarily while programs are running', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', NULL, 946, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_00947', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Multiple levels of cache memory are used to perform tasks in modern computers. Out of most cache memory units are located in .......................... . .................. cache memory is the fastest and the highest expensive cache memory', '["Main first level(L1)", "second level(L2)", "third level(L3)", "first level(L1)", "Mother third level(L3)"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Multiple levels of cache memory are used in modern computers to improve performance by reducing the average time to access data from the main memory. The cache memory hierarchy typically consists of three L1, L2, and L3', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', NULL, 947, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_00948', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'What is the primary function of the BIOS (Basic Input Output System) in a computer system?', '["Managing peripheral devices such as keyboards and mouse", "Storing user data and files", "Controlling the startup process and initializing hardware components", "Providing access to the Internet", "Executing application software"]'::jsonb, 3, 'BIOS is responsible for controlling the initial startup process of the which includes initializing hardware components such as the storage and other peripherals', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', NULL, 948, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_00949', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which tool is commonly used for reading handwritten or printed text for data processing?', '["OMR (Optical Mark Recognition)", "OCR (Optical Character Recognition)", "MICR (Magnetic Ink Character Recognition)", "Bar code readers", "Sensors and loggers"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Correct answer: "OCR (Optical Character Recognition)". This reflects how this hardware component/device is defined and used in a standard computer system.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', NULL, 949, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_00950', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of the following statements about the memory hierarchy is correct?', '["Cache memory has higher capacity but lower cost per bit than RAM", "RAM is non-volatile and retains data even without power. RAM", "Hard disk has lower cost per bit but slower access time than RAM", "Optical disks are faster than cache memory but more expensive", "Flash memory is volatile and loses data when power is off"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Cache is faster but most expensive per RAM is fast but Hard disk is slower but Optical disks are slower than hard and Flash is non-volatile. Cache', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', NULL, 950, 'A/L Past Paper Series')
