('alict_00951', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'In the ALU works closely with other registers. Which of the following statements is correct?', '["The ALU stores the next instruction to be executed", "The ALU retrieves instructions directly from RAM. ALU RAM", "The ALU performs and results are often stored in the Accumulator. ALU", "The ALU is responsible for decoding instructions before execution", "The ALU controls the timing of all CPU operations. CPU"]'::jsonb, 3, 'The ALU (Arithmetic Logic Unit) is like the CPU''s calculator. Its only job is to do math (like adding and subtracting) and compare numbers. ALU (Arithmetic Logic Unit) CPU The Accumulator is a special holding spot right next to the ALU', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', NULL, 951, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_00952', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of the following correctly matches the computer hardware component to its primary function?', '["CPU - Processes data and instructions", "RAM - Permanent data storage", "Hard Drive - Temporary data storage during processing", "GPU - Controls input devices like keyboard and mouse GPU -", "Power Supply - Stores system firmware"]'::jsonb, 1, '2025/08/27 Information and Communication Technology • CPU (Central Processing Unit): Executes instructions and processes data. CPU • RAM (Random Access Memory): volatile memory for data and instructions currently in use', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', NULL, 952, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
